    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d880">

                <pb facs="1292" n="1276" sameAs="frus:frus1949v06/pg1276"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/8–249: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic"> Mr. Paul A. Porter to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lausanne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-02T15:00:00+01:00">August 2, 1949—3
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Palun 260. Reference Palun 253.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d880-f1"/> In meeting with
                    PCC August 2 Arab delegates accepted conditions set by Israelis as basis for
                    discussion refugee problem. Delegates demonstrated cooperative attitude.</p>
                <p> PCC immediately proceeding meet Shiloah obtain for transmission Arab delegations
                    terms Israeli proposal re refugees.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Porter</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d880-f1" n="1" xml:id="d880-f1-content">
                <p>Dated July 28, from Lausanne, <ref target="#pg1266">p. 1266</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
